    "finding": "Phase 2 deliverable status: NONE OF THE THREE APPROACHES CLOSES.\n  A. 6-term sum: proton sum is sign-indefinite (-4.77); D/T/³He T2+T3 are 10^5..10^6 (out of scale).\n  B. Categorical ratio: predicts m_p/m_e ≈ 2.135 vs CODATA 1836 (factor 860 off — missing the higher T_k structure).\n  C. Placeholder ratio: hits CODATA-(m_p - m_e)/m_e to ~470 ppb, NOT m_p/m_e — hidden algebraic +1 (audit doc 2026-05-09-proton-m_e-anomaly.md).\n\nRecommended forward path: a Path A *partial* chain — T1 (canonical Wenzl-bridge anchor) + T4 (Frobenius per-vortex) only — quarantining T2 (single-pole), T3 (pair-pole), T5 (chirality-BW), T6 (Habiro residue) until each closes individually.  Currently T1+T4 yields:\n    proton:      +1.1458\n    neutron:     +0.9877\n    deuteron:    +0.5752\nNote: T1+T4 ratio (proton/neutron) ~ 1.022 vs CODATA m_p/m_n ~ 0.999 (off by 2.3%) — confirming T1+T4 alone is not the right closure either, but is the cleanest currently-trustable subset.\n\nNEXT STEPS:\n  1. Rederive T2 (single-pole brane tower) at q_0 using canonical Wenzl-bridge weight; compare to the current 6-term mpfr witness values which use the legacy weight (factor-of-2 issue same root cause as habiro_interpolate_cross_validator).\n  2. Audit T5 (chirality-BW) for sign convention — current value -7.79 dominates but with the wrong sign would give the right scale.\n  3. Once T2..T6 are individually closed, replace the placeholders with sum-derived values and re-run applied_uniqueness_mass_table.py.",
